---
description: Use verified-source research for papers, math, coding audits and evidence-based technical tutoring/curriculum lessons.
alwaysApply: false
---

For research-heavy code edits, explanations, research surveys, or curriculum/lesson authoring, read the installed `evidence-first-technical-research/SKILL.md` and related references. Use primary evidence and pinned revisions, audit equations, trace actual code, and separate confirmed behavior from hypothesis. Do not claim tests or benchmarks ran unless executed.

For teaching: design a prerequisite DAG with checkable objectives; research each lesson before teaching from first principles; one lesson per requested turn; keep objective proficiency separate from lesson delivery. Require observed learner evidence for `demonstrated`. For long-chat bias or disputed claims, cold-read and recheck primary sources before resuming. If the skill path is unavailable, say so rather than pretending it was loaded.
